Files: usr/lib/sysctl.d/70-sparky-stereo.conf, usr/lib/udev/rules.d/60-sparky-block.rules
  The values for vm.watermark_boost_factor, vm.compaction_proactiveness,
  kernel.split_lock_mitigate, vm.page-cluster and the 256 KiB read-ahead
  reproduce, as settings, what the CachyOS kernel changes by patch. The authors
  are those of the commits in the CachyOS Linux tree (read on 2026-10-08 from
  its topic branches): Sultan Alsawaf ("Disable watermark boosting by default",
  "Disable proactive compaction by default"), Eric Naim ("Disable split lock
  mitigation by default", "Disable swap-in readahead", "Increase
  VM_READAHEAD_PAGES to 256K"). No code of those patches is included.
  The value vm.max_map_count = 2147483642 is the one SteamOS (Valve Corporation)
  sets, as reported in the Fedora FESCo discussion
  https://pagure.io/fesco/issue/2993 ; SteamOS's own repository is not
  publicly readable, so its authors could not be verified and are not named.
  License: GPL-3+

